## Element templates

- `scripts/generate-element-templates.py` — **nothing hand-copied**. Downloads Camunda's official
  `agenticai-aiagent-outbound-connector.json` and `agenticai-aiagent-job-worker.json` for the exact
  `<version.connectors>` in `pom.xml` from GitHub raw, then applies a small reviewable set of edits:
  new template id/name (`com.anthrobyte.connectors.aiagent[.jobworker].org-bedrock.v1`,
  "AI Agent Task / Sub-process (Organization Bedrock Gateway)"), task-definition type → the custom
  job type, provider dropdown reduced to AWS Bedrock and hidden, Bedrock authentication pinned to
  `defaultCredentialsChain` and hidden with access key / secret key / API key fields removed, custom
  endpoint made **required** with an optional `--gateway-url` default. Records a
  `metadata.derivedFrom {id, connectorsVersion}`. Everything else (region, model, parameters,
  timeout, prompts, tools, memory, limits, events, response, retries) is left exactly as shipped.
  CLI: `--task-type --subprocess-type --gateway-url --connectors-version --source-dir --output-dir`.
- Commit the two generated files under `element-templates/`.

